  "summary": "Monday 10/26 St. Brigid CT list prepared under RBC-RAD-07. Four studies were booked; the 3 cancelled appointments (pt-0048, pt-0012, pt-0050) got no orders.\n\n1) Britt Mohr (pt-0047), CT A/P with contrast, 08:00. Order sr-t0001. Diet-controlled diabetes, and the 9/24 creatinine was more than 30 days old, so I ordered a creatinine before the scan (sr-t0009). Outside results arrived while I worked: creatinine 1.04 (10/21) to 1.52 (10/22), which is acute kidney injury. So I kept the pre-scan creatinine and added 0.9% saline 500 mL IV at 07:00 (mr-t0023). Updated patient message (arrive 06:45). Radiologist told; AKI follow-up task to Dr. Okafor (task-t0029).\n\n2) Daniel Ferreira (pt-0015), CT A/P with contrast, 09:00. Order sr-t0002. The 2019 radiology report grades his iohexol reaction as moderate, though the allergy list says \"anaphylaxis\" from his own account. So: prednisone 50 mg at 20:00/02:00/08:00 (mr-t0005) and diphenhydramine 50 mg at 08:00 (mr-t0006); he needs a driver. The lab later corrected his 10/14 creatinine from 0.98 to 2.8 (eGFR ~24), so I added saline 500 mL IV at 08:00 (mr-t0022). Corrected Spanish/English message to him (arrive 07:45), radiologist told, follow-up task to Dr. Okafor (task-t0028).\n\n3) Anisha Schuster (pt-0049), CT A/P with contrast, 13:00. Order sr-t0003. Kidney injury from her 10/04 ED visit has not resolved. Ordered: pre-scan creatinine (sr-t0010), saline 500 mL IV at 12:00 (mr-t0007), metformin on hold for the scan day and 48 h after (mr-00392), and a restart/recheck task (task-t0015). An outside 2022 report then showed a moderate reaction to iopamidol, so I added prednisone 50 mg at 00:00/06:00/12:00 (mr-t0020) and diphenhydramine 50 mg at 12:00 (mr-t0021); she needs a driver. Corrected patient message (arrive 11:45), radiologist told. Iopamidol couldn't be coded in the allergy list; the note asks for it to be added by hand.\n\n4) Lauren Beahan (pt-0046), CT A/P without contrast, 14:00. Order sr-t0004, placed as booked; patient told no prep needed. An outside report showed a prior mild iohexol reaction. I added it to her allergy list (alg-t0024); her non-contrast scan is unchanged.\n\nNotes and addenda are in each chart, and the 4 new inbox items are closed. Older inbox items for other patients were left alone.",
